---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../../../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../../../components/Footer.astro';
import StudioModal from '../../../../components/StudioModal.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Full Story — Jiří J. Stodůlka · Adaptive Studio"
  description="The personal story of the Adaptive Studio founder. From accident through burnout to conscious nervous system regulation."
  lang="en"
>
  <StudioModal lang="en" />
  <Nav lang="en" />

  <main>

    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="min-h-screen flex flex-col justify-center px-6 sm:px-10 lg:px-20 py-24">
      <p class="text-[10px] tracking-[0.4em] uppercase text-sage mb-10">FOUNDER'S STORY</p>
      <h1 class="font-heading font-bold leading-[0.9] tracking-tight text-zinc-900 mb-10 reveal"
          style="font-size: clamp(4rem, 12vw, 10rem)">
        Full Story
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed max-w-xl reveal reveal-delay-1">
        Jiří J. Stodůlka<br>
        <span class="text-sm text-zinc-400">Founder, Adaptive Studio</span>
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Chapter 01 -->
    <section class="bg-[#111110] flex flex-col px-6 sm:px-10 lg:px-20 py-24">
      <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-[1fr_2fr] gap-16 lg:gap-24">
        <div class="reveal">
          <p class="font-heading font-bold text-zinc-700 leading-none select-none"
             style="font-size: clamp(6rem, 14vw, 12rem)">01</p>
          <p class="text-[10px] tracking-[0.4em] uppercase text-sage mt-4">CHAPTER</p>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal reveal-delay-1">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight mb-10">
            I didn't want to slow down.
          </h2>
          <div class="space-y-5 text-zinc-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-10">
            <p>I've always been physically active. Always at the limit — and always beyond it. Attention deficits led to avoidable injuries. I didn't understand the signals of exhaustion. And honestly — I didn't want to hear them.</p>
            <p>In my early twenties, a dirt bike accident nearly killed me. I lost my spleen, broke several bones, and suffered nerve damage in my right arm. Still — within two years, I was racing again. The paralysis never fully healed.</p>
          </div>
          <blockquote class="border-l-2 border-sage pl-6">
            <p class="font-heading text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white leading-tight">
              The limits I kept pushing gave me a false sense of fulfilment. They masked a destructive pattern.
            </p>
          </blockquote>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Chapter 02 -->
    <section class="bg-[#111110] flex flex-col px-6 sm:px-10 lg:px-20 py-24 border-t border-zinc-800">
      <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-[1fr_2fr] gap-16 lg:gap-24">
        <div class="reveal">
          <p class="font-heading font-bold text-zinc-700 leading-none select-none"
             style="font-size: clamp(6rem, 14vw, 12rem)">02</p>
          <p class="text-[10px] tracking-[0.4em] uppercase text-sage mt-4">CHAPTER</p>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal reveal-delay-1">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight mb-10">
            Functional on the outside.<br>Collapsing within.
          </h2>
          <div class="space-y-5 text-zinc-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-10">
            <p>I completed two university degrees with a nervous system as tense as a trauma survivor's. Outwardly: highly functional. Inwardly: a ticking time bomb.</p>
            <p>In 2018, I immigrated to Canada. A career in AI as a Data Scientist. Two freelance projects. Building one of the most active AI communities in North America. COVID. All at once. Waking up at night seeing code from the day before. Old injuries began screaming.</p>
            <p>We returned to Europe. I shifted to a management role. I couldn't even look at a screen. I was completely depleted. But I was a father now. Stopping was not an option.</p>
            <p>In 2025, I broke again. This time it felt life-threatening. A dysregulated autonomic nervous system — I could barely breathe. People around me began asking if I had considered suicide. That terrified me — not because I had, but because they had lost hope. And so had I.</p>
          </div>
          <blockquote class="border-l-2 border-sage pl-6">
            <p class="font-heading text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white leading-tight">
              I knew I had to act differently. So I did the one thing I should have done twelve years earlier: I stopped.
            </p>
          </blockquote>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Chapter 03 -->
    <section class="bg-[#111110] flex flex-col px-6 sm:px-10 lg:px-20 py-24 border-t border-zinc-800">
      <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-[1fr_2fr] gap-16 lg:gap-24">
        <div class="reveal">
          <p class="font-heading font-bold text-zinc-700 leading-none select-none"
             style="font-size: clamp(6rem, 14vw, 12rem)">03</p>
          <p class="text-[10px] tracking-[0.4em] uppercase text-sage mt-4">CHAPTER</p>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal reveal-delay-1">
          <h2 class="font-heading text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight mb-10">
            I learned to regulate.
          </h2>
          <div class="space-y-5 text-zinc-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-10">
            <p>I got lucky. I met people who didn't let me drown. They introduced me to ancient, simple, yet powerful practices: breathwork and meditation. Three times a day for a month. Slowly, I began to breathe again — really breathe.</p>
            <p>And then I learned something I had never known: self-regulation. A basic human skill. But its absence had cost me everything. As I learned to regulate my nervous system, my senses awakened. For the first time in my life, I could truly feel my body.</p>
            <p>I decided: I would suppress nothing anymore. No matter how difficult — the only way out of pain is through it. Resilience isn't just endurance. It is the art of rebuilding a life worth living.</p>
          </div>
          <blockquote class="border-l-2 border-sage pl-6">
            <p class="font-heading text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white leading-tight">
              Adaptive Studio is the result of that decision. And now I've made another one: to help others live in a way they never have to walk the path I did.
            </p>
          </blockquote>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section class="min-h-[50vh] flex flex-col items-center justify-center px-6 text-center py-24">
      <div class="reveal">
        <h2 class="font-heading font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight text-zinc-900 mb-8"
            style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 4rem)">
          Ready to train your regulation?
        </h2>
        <a
          href="https://calendly.com/jiri-adaptivestudio/30min"
          class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-12 py-5 bg-zinc-900 text-white text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.2em] uppercase hover:bg-zinc-700 transition-colors duration-200"
        >
          Book a consultation
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>

  <Footer lang="en" />
</Layout>

<script>
  const observer = new IntersectionObserver(
    (entries) => {
      entries.forEach((entry) => {
        if (entry.isIntersecting) entry.target.classList.add('visible');
      });
    },
    { threshold: 0.05, rootMargin: '0px 0px -5% 0px' }
  );

  document.querySelectorAll('.reveal').forEach((el) => {
    const rect = el.getBoundingClientRect();
    if (rect.top < window.innerHeight) {
      el.classList.add('visible');
    } else {
      observer.observe(el);
    }
  });
</script>
